WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.840
Welcome to the payroll voucher deep-dive.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.525
Before SaloneHCM, branches emailed spreadsheets or carried paper vouchers to headquarters.

3
00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:17.369
Now, every branch submits into one central digital repository, and every voucher passes a strict approval chain before a single leone moves.

4
00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:19.138
Let's walk the full journey.

5
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.116
This is the central repository.

6
00:00:22.116 --> 00:00:32.527
The indicator cards show how many branches have submitted this period, what's awaiting supervisor sign-off, what's in finance review, and what's been authorised for payment.

7
00:00:32.527 --> 00:00:36.138
Filters let you slice by period, branch, and workflow stage.

8
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:11.958
Open any voucher and you see the full story: every employee line with gross pay, P A Y E, NASSIT, loan deductions and net pay; the totals; and the complete audit timeline — who created it, who approved it, and exactly when.

9
00:01:11.958 --> 00:01:14.171
Once submitted, a voucher is frozen.

10
00:01:14.171 --> 00:01:16.322
Nobody can quietly change a number.

11
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.955
The workflow enforces four eyes at minimum.

12
00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:24.541
A branch officer submits. The branch supervisor approves.

13
00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:32.720
A finance officer reviews and approves — and the system physically blocks anyone from approving a voucher they created themselves.

14
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:41.591
Finally a Ministry of Finance approver authorises payment — and that person must be different from both the creator and the finance approver.

15
00:01:41.591 --> 00:01:44.674
Dual control, enforced by software, not by trust.

16
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:55.055
Mistakes happen. Instead of editing in place, a reviewer returns the voucher with a written reason — at least ten characters, always recorded.

17
00:01:55.055 --> 00:01:59.954
The branch corrects the figures, resubmits, and the revision number increments.

18
00:01:59.954 --> 00:02:02.186
The correction history is permanent.

19
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:08.713
And the quiet protections: one voucher per branch per period — duplicates are rejected.

20
00:02:08.713 --> 00:02:14.364
An employee cannot appear on two vouchers in the same month — that's the double-pay guard.

21
00:02:14.364 --> 00:02:19.451
And once payment is authorised, the voucher becomes a permanent immutable record.

22
00:02:19.451 --> 00:02:22.402
This is how payroll fraud loopholes get closed.

23
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.812
Submit digitally, approve in chain, return with reasons, and let the rails do their work.

24
00:02:28.812 --> 00:02:32.874
The voucher certification quiz awaits you in the Training Center.
